<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yewe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yewe is a secret religious order of the Ewe of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togo">Togo</a>, devoted to the thunder god Xevieso and related deities. Its initiates took new names, followed strict rules and used a language of their own, and the order became a powerful society that influenced Anlo politics in the 19th century. Missionaries and colonial authorities tried to suppress it.</p></div>
